<item>
  <title>Day 4: nf-core pipelines</title>
  <link>https://your-website-url.example.com/posts/day4/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 






<p>nf-core is a community built around nextflow, where people build nextflow pipelines on different bioinformatics data.</p>
<section id="why-use-nf-core" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="why-use-nf-core">why use nf-core?</h2>
<p>When we want to analyse data, we can be pretty sure that a pipeline for that type of data probably already exists. So we can save time and effort by using an already validated pipeline, built and maintained by an expert. We also get all the benefits of nextflow, like reproducibility and portability.</p>
</section>
<section id="setup" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="setup">setup</h2>
<p>So now all we have to do is to create a pixi environment containing nextflow and nf-core:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode bash code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb1-1"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">pixi</span> init nextflow_test <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-c</span> conda-forge <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-c</span> bioconda</span>
<span id="cb1-2"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">cd</span> nextflow_test</span>
<span id="cb1-3"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">pixi</span> add nextflow nf-core</span></code></pre></div></div>
</section>
<section id="test-run" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="test-run">test run</h2>
<p>In this example, we will use the Sarek pipeline:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb2" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode bash code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb2-1"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">pixi</span> run nextflow run nf-core/sarek <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-profile</span> test <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--outdir</span> sarek_test <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-c</span> hpc2n.config</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>hpc2n.config is a configuration file that we need to run this pipeline on our cluster!</p>
</section>
<section id="running-nf-core-pipeline-on-real-data" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="running-nf-core-pipeline-on-real-data">running nf-core pipeline on real data!</h2>
<p>We first made a samplesheet with the samples we wanted to analyse. Then we added it to the form on the nf-core launcher and ran it as a batch job:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb3" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode bash code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb3-1"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">pixi</span> run nextflow run nf-core/rnaseq <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-r</span> 3.26.0 <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-params-file</span> nf-params.json <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-c</span> hpc2n.config</span></code></pre></div></div>


</section>

 ]]></description>
