<item>
  <title>Day 2: Pixi, quality control and containers</title>
  <link>https://your-website-url.example.com/posts/Day2/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 






<p>A problem with reproducible research is that different software versions and dependencies can lead to very different results. So how do we solve this?</p>
<section id="pixi" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="pixi">Pixi</h2>
<p>Pixi is an environment manager that we can run on all major operating systems. Pixi installs tools and dependencies in one project, so that others can reproduce the same results.</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode bash code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb1-1"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">pixi</span> init myproject <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-c</span> conda-forge <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-c</span> bioconda   <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># conda-forge first!</span></span>
<span id="cb1-2"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">cd</span> myproject</span>
<span id="cb1-3"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">pixi</span> add fastqc multiqc</span>
<span id="cb1-4"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">pixi</span> run fastqc <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--help</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
</section>
<section id="pixi-file-structure" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="pixi-file-structure">pixi file structure</h2>
<p>But what are the files that we now have in the project? pixi.toml lists the channels, platforms and dependencies. pixi.lock records the exact versions of the dependencies and is not to be ever deleted!</p>
</section>
<section id="quality-control" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="quality-control">quality control</h2>
<p>In bioinformatics, quality control is a fundamental step to make sure that the data is of good quality. One way to do this is using FastQC, a tool that generates a report with quality metrics.</p>
<p>We ran fastqc on the samples and then used MultiQC to summarize the results in one report.</p>
</section>
<section id="containers" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="containers">containers</h2>
<p>Containers are built as container images that specify the operating system, dependencies, and software in an isolated environment. The container management tool then takes the images and build the container. These management tools can be run on all operating systems and it will run in all environments.</p>
<p>To download container images, we could use for example dockerhub or seqera.</p>
<p>We then used apptainer to get the image with apptainer pulland run the software inside the container with apptainer exec.:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb2" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode bash code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb2-1"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">apptainer</span> pull fastqc_0.12.1.sif docker://biocontainers/fastqc:v0.11.9_cv8</span>
<span id="cb2-2"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">apptainer</span> exec fastqc_0.12.1.sif fastqc <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--version</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
</section>
<section id="running-containers-with-sbatch" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="running-containers-with-sbatch">running containers with sbatch</h2>
<p>We can run apptainer containers as part of a batch job. Example:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb3" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode bash code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb3-1"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">#! /bin/bash -l</span></span>
<span id="cb3-2"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">#SBATCH -A project_ID</span></span>
<span id="cb3-3"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">#SBATCH -t 30:00</span></span>
<span id="cb3-4"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">#SBATCH -n 1</span></span>
<span id="cb3-5"></span>
<span id="cb3-6"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">apptainer</span> exec container_image.sif fastqc <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-o</span> . <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--noextract</span> ../data/<span class="pp" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">*</span>fastq.gz</span></code></pre></div></div>


</section>

 ]]></description>
