<item>
  <title>Day 1: How to make a Quarto blog</title>
  <link>https://your-website-url.example.com/posts/Day1/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 






<section id="purpose-of-this-blog" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="purpose-of-this-blog">purpose of this blog</h2>
<p>The purpose of this blog is to document this course. It is both a way to review my notes, especially the most complex parts, and a way to practice my skills in Quarto.</p>
</section>
<section id="creating-the-blog" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="creating-the-blog">creating the blog</h2>
<p>Creating the blog was actually fairly easy. All we need to do is open VScode and create a new project. Then, we select the Quarto blog and that’s it! The blog skeleton is created and we can now personalise it.</p>
</section>
<section id="blog-structure" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="blog-structure">blog structure</h2>
<p>We will have one post for every day of the course, so five in total. What we need to do for this is have a “posts” folder where we will create a new folder for every day. There, we will write inside the index.qmd file, which contains the content of this post.</p>
</section>
<section id="publishing-it-on-github" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="publishing-it-on-github">publishing it on github</h2>
<p>First, we create a new repository on github. Then:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode bash code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb1-1"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">git</span> init</span>
<span id="cb1-2"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">git</span> add .</span>
<span id="cb1-3"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">git</span> commit <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-m</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Initial blog"</span></span>
<span id="cb1-4"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">git</span> remote add origin https://github.com/<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;</span>user<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&gt;</span>/<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;</span>repo<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&gt;</span>.git</span>
<span id="cb1-5"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">git</span> branch <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-M</span> main</span>
<span id="cb1-6"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">git</span> push <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-u</span> origin main</span></code></pre></div></div>


</section>

 ]]></description>
